# `raw_string_delimiter` is external and it is the whole point of a C++ raw
# string: the closer is not `)"` but `)tag"`, chosen per literal. The content
# here contains `)b`, which is a closer for the empty delimiter and not for
# this one.
#
# The first draft of this specimen was `R"tag(a)b"tag"`, which has no closer
# at all; tree-sitter ERRORed on it and that is how I learned my authored
# input was wrong rather than outliner. An oracle that refuses is worth more
# than an oracle that agrees.
roots 1
mends 0
holds raw_string_delimiter
spans raw_string_delimiter 18 21
spans raw_string_delimiter 26 29
holds raw_string_content
spans raw_string_content 22 25
